    "note": "**αὐτὸς** (the/this/who) is emphatic — the pronoun is explicitly stated when Greek verbs already encode the subject. **ταῦτα** (object) is fronted before the verb for emphasis. **αὐτὸς** is emphatic — the pronoun is explicitly stated when Greek verbs already encode the subject. **αὐτὸς** is emphatic — the pronoun is explicitly stated when Greek verbs already encode the subject. **αὐτὸς** is emphatic — the pronoun is explicitly stated when Greek verbs already encode the subject."
